# Shared model facts injected into BOTH engines at deploy time (single source of truth).
# deploy.sh sources this for `--model qwen3.6-35b-a3b` and injects the values, so the vLLM values
# and the SGLang manifest cannot drift.
#
# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: a 256-expert MoE with 8 experts per token, so about 3B parameters are active
# for every token against 35B stored. That ratio is the reason to try it here. The workload this
# serves is agentic and reads far more than it writes -- 99.5% of the tokens in a measured
# SWE-bench episode were prompt -- and prefill is compute-bound, so cutting the active FLOPs per
# token is the lever that moves the box's throughput. Whether it moves it by the ratio is a
# measurement, not a claim; see FACTS.md.
#
# The official FP8 checkpoint is served rather than the bf16 base: 35B in fp8 is about 35 GiB and
# leaves room for KV on four L40S, and this checkpoint keeps the vision tower in higher precision.
MODEL_ID=Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B
NATIVE_CONTEXT=262144
YARN_FACTOR=4
